decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">h</span> : <span class=\"fn\">0</span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#LT.lt\">&lt;</a> <span class=\"fn\">b</span>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Data/Int/Linear.html#Int.Internal.Linear.cmod\">cmod</a> <span class=\"fn\">a</span> <span class=\"fn\">b</span></span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#GT.gt\">&gt;</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Neg.neg\">-</a><span class=\"fn\">b</span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"","docLink":"./Init/Data/Int/Linear.html#Int.Internal.Linear.cmod_gt_of_pos","kind":"theorem","line":253,"name":"Int.Internal.Linear.cmod_gt_of_pos","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/6a10ac8c22beadecabdbb0919c2b50214762f91d/src/Init/Data/Int/Linear.lean#L253-L254"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">theorem</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Init/Data/Int/Linear.html#Int.Internal.Linear.cdiv_add_cmod\"><span class=\"name\">Int</span>.<span class=\"name\">Internal</span>.<span class=\"name\">Linear</span>.<span class=\"name\">cdiv_add_cmod</span></a></span><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">a </span><span class=\"fn\">b</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Data/Int/Basic.html#Int\">Int</a>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\">b</span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#HMul.hMul\">*</a> <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Data/Int/Linear.html#Int.Internal.Linear.cdiv\">cdiv</a> <span class=\"fn\">a</span> <span class=\"fn\">b</span></span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#HAdd.hAdd\">+</a> <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Data/Int/Linear.html#Int.Internal.Linear.cmod\">cmod</a> <span class=\"fn\">a</span> <span class=\"fn\">b</span></span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Eq\">=</a> <span class=\"fn\">a</span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"","docLink":"./Init/Data/Int/Linear.html#Int.Internal.Linear.cdiv_add_cmod","kind":"theorem","line":245,"name":"Int.Internal.Linear.cdiv_add_cmod","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/6a10ac8c22beadecabdbb0919c2b50214762f91d/src/Init/Data/Int/Linear.lean#L245-L251"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Init/Data/Int/Linear.html#Int.Internal.Linear.cmod\"><span class=\"name\">Int</span>.<span class=\"name\">Internal</span>.<span class=\"name\">Linear</span>.<span class=\"name\">cmod</span></a></span><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">a </span><span class=\"fn\">b</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Data/Int/Basic.html#Int\">Int</a>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Data/Int/Basic.html#Int\">Int</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Returns the ceiling-compatible remainder of the division `a / b`.\nThis function ensures that the remainder is consistent with `cdiv`, meaning:\n```\na = b * cdiv a b + cmod a b\n```\nSee theorem `cdiv_add_cmod`. We also have\n```\n-b < cmod a b ≤ 0\n```\n","docLink":"./Init/Data/Int/Linear.html#Int.Internal.Linear.cmod","kind":"def","line":230,"name":"Int.Internal.Linear.cmod","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/6a10ac8c22beadecabdbb0919c2b50214762f91d/src/Init/Data/Int/Linear.lean#L230-L243"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Init/Data/Int/Linear.html#Int.Internal.Linear.cdiv\"><span class=\"name\">Int</span>.<span class=\"name\">Internal</span>.<span class=\"name\">Linear</span>.<span class=\"name\">cdiv</span></a></span><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">a </span><span class=\"fn\">b</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Data/Int/Basic.html#Int\">Int</a>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Data/Int/Basic.html#Int\">Int</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Returns the ceiling of the division `a / b`. That is, the result is equivalent to `⌈a / b⌉`.\nExamples:\n- `cdiv 7 3` returns `3`\n- `cdiv (-7) 3` returns `-2`.\n","docLink":"./Init/Data/Int/Linear.html#Int.Internal.Linear.cdiv","kind":"def","line":220,"name":"Int.Internal.Linear.cdiv","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/6a10ac8c22beadecabdbb0919c2b50214762f91d/src/Init/Data/Int/Linear.lean#L220-L228"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Init/Data/Int/Linear.html#Int.Internal.Linear.Expr.norm\"><span class=\"name\">Int</span>.<span class=\"name\">Internal</span>.<span class=\"name\">Linear</span>.<span class=\"name\">Expr</span>.<span class=\"name\">norm</span></a></span><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">e</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Data/Int/Linear.html#Int.Internal.Linear.Expr\">Expr</a>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Data/Int/Linear.html#Int.Internal.Linear.Poly\">Poly</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Converts the given expression into a polynomial, and then normalizes it. ","docLink":"./Init/Data/Int/Linear.html#Int.Internal.Linear.Expr.norm","kind":"def","line":215,"name":"Int.Internal.Linear.Expr.norm","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/6a10ac8c22beadecabdbb0919c2b50214762f91d/src/Init/Data/Int/Linear.lean#L215-L218"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Init/Data/Int/Linear.html#Int.Internal.Linear.Expr.toPoly'.go\"><span class=\"name\">Int</span>.<span class=\"name\">Internal</span>.<span class=\"name\">Linear</span>.<span class=\"name\">Expr</span>.<span class=\"name\">toPoly'</span>.<span class=\"name\">go</span></a></span><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"f